Fix crashes and hangs on coplanar input (OpenMeshCraft @0e8d12c3).

- Triangulation::createTPI: planes[1]/planes[2] were left uninitialized when every
  triangle listed with a segment is coplanar with the triangle being split (a segment
  on an edge of a coplanar triangle is only listed with the triangles whose interior
  it crosses). The TPI was then built from stack garbage: an out-of-range read, or a
  degenerate point (d == 0) whose predicates return NaN and reach OMC_EXIT. Initialize
  the planes, test coplanarity exactly instead of only by the coplanar list, and use
  the plane through the segment's source edge and a point off the triangle's plane
  when no supporting triangle qualifies.
- remove_duplicates(tbb::concurrent_vector): shrinking with resize() frees segments of
  the reserved first block, and a later push_back into them spins forever (oneTBB
  2021.5 - 2022.1). Clear and refill instead.
- OMC_EXIT: throw OMC::RuntimeError instead of calling std::exit(), so the host
  application gets a failed boolean instead of being terminated. The SSI constructor
  calls OMC_EXIT and was noexcept, where a throw calls std::terminate(); drop the
  noexcept.
- IntervalNumber::operator/: the scalar SSE2 path (no AVX, no SSE4.1) declared the
  rounding protector twice; GCC rejects the redeclaration. Pre-existing, but only
  reached once AVX is off.

